sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor Alice as alice (rules:author)
  actor Bob as bob (rules:approve)
  participant API as rule-engine-rest
  participant SVC as VersionService
  participant DB as PostgreSQL (rle_version)
  participant SCH as Scheduler thread (any replica)

  Alice->>API: PUT /rule-sets/card-fee/versions/2 (If-Match "4")
  API->>SVC: updateDraft
  SVC->>DB: UPDATE ... WHERE status='DRAFT' AND lock_version=4
  Alice->>API: POST /rule-sets/card-fee/versions/2:request-publish {effectiveFrom 2027-01-01}
  SVC->>DB: validate, status=PENDING_APPROVAL, requested_by=alice, COMMIT
  SVC-->>Alice: 200, event rules.version.publish-requested.v1

  Alice->>API: POST .../versions/2:approve
  API->>SVC: approve(approver=alice)
  SVC-->>Alice: 403 SELF_APPROVAL_FORBIDDEN (requested_by == approver)

  Bob->>API: GET /rule-sets/card-fee/versions/1/diff/2
  API-->>Bob: added, removed, changed rows
  Bob->>API: POST .../versions/2:approve (Idempotency-Key, If-Match "5")
  API->>SVC: approve(approver=bob)
  alt bob != requested_by and status PENDING_APPROVAL
    SVC->>DB: status=PUBLISHED, approved_by=bob, cache_epoch+1, COMMIT, pg_notify
    SVC-->>Bob: 200, event rules.version.published.v1
  else stale If-Match or already approved
    SVC-->>Bob: 409 VERSION_CONFLICT or 409 INVALID_STATE
  end

  Note over DB,SCH: Evaluation picks the version whose effective_from <= clock, so v2 applies from 2027-01-01 without any wake-up
  SCH->>DB: at 2027-01-01: UPDATE v1 status=RETIRED, COMMIT
  SCH-->>SCH: event rules.version.retired.v1
